msgid "training.guide"
msgstr "About this screen"

msgid "training.home.guide"
msgstr "These controls work on the battle you are in. Dummy Recording records pad input onto the dummy and plays it back. Input History lists what each player pressed. Combo creator writes combos down, replays them for you and checks your own attempts as trials. F6 opens and closes the controls, the arrows move, Enter selects and Esc goes back a screen."

msgid "training.recording.guide"
msgstr "Pick a slot, then Record: Player 1's pad drives the dummy until you stop. Play has the dummy repeat the slot, and Loop keeps it repeating. F7 starts and stops a recording without opening this screen. Slots last for this battle only; Save recording keeps one as a named file and Load recording brings it back."

msgid "training.history.guide"
msgstr "Each player's pad inputs, newest first, with the frames each one was held. Select a player to read the list. It shows what was pressed, not which move came out."

msgid "training.combo.guide"
msgstr "1. The fighter on top is Player 1's; its packs and combos are the rows under it. 2. Put the moves on the Moves line: type them, or use Record combo and perform the combo. 3. Add as new combo keeps it in the pack. 4. Edit moves changes it row by row, Edit timing shifts single moves by frames, Replay moves plays it for you. 5. Start trial checks your own attempts. Every row explains itself while it is highlighted."

msgid "training.combo.timing.guide"
msgstr "One row a move. Left and Right on a move shift its press a frame earlier or later (@N). Replay moves plays the combo, and each row then says what the replay saw: how long it waited and whether the move connected. F8 on a move replays up to that move. Add, Duplicate and Remove work on the move you highlighted last; on a move's row Insert, D and Delete do the same."

msgid "training.combo.moves"
msgstr "Edit moves"

msgid "training.combo.moves.detail"
msgstr "The combo's moves beside the moves you can add: drag moves in, reorder them, change a move's strength, stance, cancel or timing, and loop a group of them."

msgid "training.combo.moves.guide"
msgstr "Left: the combo, a move a row. Middle: the selected move and what can be changed about it. Right: the moves you can add. Drag a move from the right onto the combo and it goes in after the move it lands on; double-click adds it after the selected move. Drag a move of the combo to give it another place. With the keys: Up and Down walk the rows, Select on a move types it anew, and on a move's row Insert adds after it, D duplicates, Delete removes, G puts it in the group. Changes are saved in the selected combo while the Moves line is that combo; otherwise they stay on the Moves line until Add combo or Save combo."

msgid "training.combo.moves.add"
msgstr "Add after move {0}"

msgid "training.combo.moves.add_first"
msgstr "Add the first move"

msgid "training.combo.moves.add.detail"
msgstr "Type one move, or several separated by >, as on the Moves line. They go in after the move you highlighted last. Insert on a move's row opens this."

msgid "training.combo.moves.duplicate"
msgstr "Duplicate move {0}"

msgid "training.combo.moves.duplicate.detail"
msgstr "Puts a copy right after the move. D on the move's row does the same."

msgid "training.combo.moves.remove"
msgstr "Remove move {0}"

msgid "training.combo.moves.remove.detail"
msgstr "Takes the move out of the combo. Delete on the move's row does the same. A combo keeps at least one move."

